course: dictionary
lesson: 4087
title: Gibbous: a word from the Moon
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Science books use special words, and some of them come from Latin. Gibbous is one. You can work out much of its meaning from the words around it. «In between we see a thin crescent, then a half moon, then a fat gibbous moon.» The order goes thin, half, then fat. So gibbous must describe a Moon that is bigger than half, but not yet full.
explain: The sentence also gives you a clue about growing and shrinking. «...a fat gibbous moon, growing (waxing) to full and then shrinking (waning) back to new.» Waxing means growing, and waning means shrinking. So a waxing gibbous moon is getting bigger, and a waning gibbous moon is getting smaller.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Does «a fat gibbous moon» still make sense if you think of it as «a bulging moon, more than half lit but not full»? Yes, it does. When a word fits the clues and the sentence still makes sense, you have probably found its meaning.
fact: Gibbous means more than half lit but not yet full, so it looks like a bulging circle.
fact: A waxing gibbous moon is growing towards full.
fact: A waning gibbous moon is shrinking back towards new.
fact: The Moon goes through its phases in about 29 and a half days.
fact: Phrases such as «waxing gibbous» and «waning gibbous» are used in science lessons about the phases of the Moon.
exercise: «In between we see a thin crescent, then a half moon, then a fat gibbous moon.» What is a gibbous moon? | *More than half lit but not yet full | Round and shining at its very brightest | Completely dark, with no light at all | A thin curved slice like a fingernail
exercise: «...a fat gibbous moon, growing (waxing) to full and then shrinking (waning) back to new.» Find and copy the word that means growing. | *waxing | waning | half | new
exercise: The Moon is a waning gibbous tonight. Is it getting bigger or smaller in the sky? | Bigger, on its way to new | Smaller, on its way to full | Bigger, on its way to full | *Smaller, on its way back to new
test: What does gibbous mean? | Lit up by the sun at midday | Completely dark | A thin curved slice of light | *Bulging, more than half lit but not full
test: In the order of the Moon's phases, which comes straight after first quarter? | New moon | Waxing crescent | *Waxing gibbous | Full moon
exam: A science book says «a waning gibbous moon». Which phrase describes the Moon on its way back to new? | *Waning gibbous | Full moon | First quarter | Waxing gibbous
